## Rules

- One row per feature the product needs. Slice IDs follow `feature-NNN-<slug>` per `04-project/harness/engineering/implementation-workflow.md`.
- *Business Goal* is one sentence in user-facing language. No technical detail.
- *Wave* is optional. Use it when the product has natural sequencing buckets (Foundation / Core / Growth / Optimization). Leave blank for small products.
- Every row carries a *Source*: `catalog v1` for the bootstrap-time catalog, or `user request YYYY-MM-DD` / `stakeholder workshop YYYY-MM-DD` for later additions. Untraceable rows are forbidden.

## Status Transitions

| From | To | Trigger |
|---|---|---|
| `planned` | `in-backlog` | Planner promotes the row to `04-project/backlog.md`. Status updates here in the same commit. |
| `in-backlog` | `in-flight` | Sprint commits the row to `sprints/<sprint>/commitments.md`. Status updates here in the same commit. |
| `in-flight` | `shipped` | Feature slice closes. Status updates here in the close-stage Product Delta. |
| any | `deprecated` | Product owner retires the feature. Row stays in this file for history; new product-roadmap entries do not reference it. |

## How AI Agent Uses This

- At cold-start, the agent surfaces the count of features in each status (planned / in-backlog / in-flight / shipped). This is **product-level visibility**, distinct from the project-level backlog count.
- When the user asks *"what's next?"* after closing a slice, the agent reads this file and proposes the lowest-wave feature with status `planned` as the next candidate for Planner promotion to backlog.
- AI Agent **does not edit this file unless instructed**. The product roadmap is owned by Product / BA Lead. AI Agent reads it, surfaces summary, and asks for explicit approval before adding/removing/reprioritizing rows.

## Update Triggers

- **Sprint 0** — first population (vision + initial catalog).
- **Product Owner adds a feature** — manual edit, with `Source` naming the trigger.
- **Slice transitions** — automatic status flip on backlog promotion, sprint commit, and slice close.
- **Quarterly review** — owner re-prioritizes waves and statuses based on user feedback and business signals.
